---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import {projects,skills,profile} from '../data/profile';
const base=import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<Layout><section class="hero wrap" aria-labelledby="hero-title"><div class="hero-top"><span class="eyebrow"><i></i> ENGINEERING CONNECTIONS</span><span class="serial">PORTFOLIO / 01</span></div><p class="role">Senior Full Stack .NET Developer</p><h1 id="hero-title">Krishna Prasad<br/><span>Namala</span><span class="name-dot">.</span></h1><div class="hero-bottom"><div><h2>Building reliable applications<br/>for a connected world.</h2><p>I design and develop enterprise applications using C#, .NET, Angular, and Azure. My work spans APIs, distributed services, responsive interfaces, and the systems that connect them.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button" href="#work">Explore My Work <span>&#8599;</span></a><a class="text-link" href="#skills">View My Expertise &#8595;</a></div></div><div class="experience"><strong>12<span> years</span></strong><p>of software development experience</p></div></div><div class="flow-art"><div class="art-label"><span>CONNECTED SERVICES</span><span>Conceptual illustration</span></div><p class="sr-only">A web application sends requests to APIs, services process business operations, and data stores persist information. Select a stage for an explanation.</p><div class="service-flow">{['Web Application','APIs','Services','Data'].map((stage,i)=><button class="stage" data-stage={i} aria-pressed={i===0?'true':'false'}><span class="node-icon">{['\u25eb','\u2318','\u25c7','\u25a4'][i]}</span><span>{stage}</span><small>0{i+1}</small></button>)}</div><p id="stage-description" aria-live="polite">Web Application — Responsive interfaces make application workflows accessible to users.</p></div></section>
<section id="work" class="wrap section"><div class="section-heading"><div><span class="eyebrow">01 / SELECTED WORK</span><h2>Complex systems.<br/><em>Clear purpose.</em></h2></div><p>An industry-focused look at application development, integration, and delivery. All work is anonymized.</p></div><div class="projects">{projects.map(p=><a class="project" href={`${base}work/${p.slug}/`}><div class={`project-art art-${p.number}`} aria-hidden="true"><span class="art-tag">CONCEPTUAL ILLUSTRATION</span><div class="diagram"><span>{p.number==='01'?'API':p.number==='02'?'UI':'ACCESS'}</span><b>&#8594;</b><span>{p.number==='01'?'EVENT':p.number==='02'?'CLOUD':'SERVICE'}</span><b>&#8594;</b><span>DATA</span></div><span class="art-index">{p.number} / SYSTEM STUDY</span></div><div class="project-content"><span class="eyebrow">{p.industry}</span><h3>{p.title}</h3><p>{p.summary}</p><div class="tags">{p.tech.slice(0,3).map(t=><span>{t}</span>)}</div><span class="read">Read Case Study &#8599;</span></div></a>)}</div><div class="additional"><span class="eyebrow">ALSO IN THE TOOLKIT / FINANCIAL SERVICES</span><h3>Modernizing Enterprise Integrations</h3><p>.NET and WCF services, XML contracts, database access, data migration, and legacy integrations, alongside React interfaces and reusable components.</p></div></section>
<section class="demo-section section" id="explorer"><div class="wrap demo-grid"><div><span class="eyebrow">02 / INTERACTIVE EXPLORATION</span><h2>Follow a request.<br/><em>Understand the flow.</em></h2><h3>Service Flow Explorer</h3><p>Portfolio demonstration using synthetic data.</p><p>This browser-only example computes a validation result and simulated response. It does not connect to a real .NET backend, client system, or Azure service.</p></div><div class="demo-panel"><div class="demo-steps" aria-label="Conceptual request flow">Request <span>&#8594;</span> Validation <span>&#8594;</span> Service <span>&#8594;</span> Response</div><form id="demo-form"><label for="sample">Synthetic sample request</label><select id="sample"><option value="valid">Valid — create a synthetic task</option><option value="invalid">Invalid — missing title and negative quantity</option></select><pre id="request">{JSON.stringify({title:'Synthetic task',quantity:2},null,2)}</pre><div class="actions"><button class="button" type="submit">Run request &#8594;</button><button type="reset" class="reset">Reset</button></div></form><p id="demo-status" role="status">Ready to validate a sample.</p><pre id="response" aria-label="Simulated response">No response yet.</pre><noscript><p>A title is required and quantity must be a positive integer. A valid sample receives a simulated 200 response; an invalid sample receives 400 with validation errors. Enable JavaScript to run this demonstration.</p></noscript></div></div></section>
<section class="wrap section" id="skills"><div class="section-heading"><div><span class="eyebrow">03 / EXPERTISE</span><h2>The tools behind<br/><em>the connections.</em></h2></div><p>Experience across the application lifecycle. Technology selection follows the problem; depth varies by project and responsibility.</p></div><div class="skills">{skills.map(([title,list,copy,slug])=><article><h3>{title}</h3><p>{copy}</p><p class="skill-list">{list}</p>{slug&&<a class="text-link" href={`${base}work/${slug}/`}>Related work &#8599;</a>}</article>)}</div><div id="approach" class="approach"><span class="eyebrow">ENGINEERING APPROACH</span><h3>Build for the people<br/>who use it. And maintain it.</h3><div><p><strong>Maintainable by design.</strong> Clear contracts, focused services, and readable code make change easier to reason about.</p><p><strong>Secure and testable.</strong> Review access boundaries, validate inputs, and test behavior at meaningful service boundaries.</p><p><strong>Ready to diagnose.</strong> Useful logs, application monitoring, and repeatable delivery support production troubleshooting.</p><p><strong>AI with accountability.</strong> Treat generated code as a draft. Review its behavior, security, and maintainability, then validate with tests.</p></div></div></section>
<section class="wrap section journey" id="journey"><div><span class="eyebrow">04 / THE JOURNEY</span><h2>A connected career.<br/><em>An enduring curiosity.</em></h2><p>I’m a full-stack developer who enjoys making complex enterprise systems easier to use, maintain, and extend. My work covers the application lifecycle—from API design and data access to responsive interfaces, cloud deployment, testing, and production support.</p></div><ol class="timeline"><li><span>FOUNDATIONS</span><h3>Applications & integration</h3><p>.NET application development, database access, and legacy service contracts in enterprise environments.</p></li><li><span>EXPANDING THE STACK</span><h3>Full-stack workflows</h3><p>Responsive interfaces, APIs, transactional applications, and reporting across industry contexts.</p></li><li><span>CONNECTING SYSTEMS</span><h3>Cloud & distributed services</h3><p>Azure applications, Angular interfaces, asynchronous processing, and production diagnostics.</p></li><li><span>CONTINUING THE PRACTICE</span><h3>Thoughtful tools. Human judgment.</h3><p>AI-assisted development supported by code review, testing, and validation.</p></li></ol></section>
<section id="contact" class="contact section"><div class="wrap"><span class="eyebrow">05 / WHAT’S NEXT</span><h2>Let’s build something<br/><em>that connects.</em><span>&#8599;</span></h2><p>Open to conversations about .NET, Azure, and full-stack engineering opportunities.</p>{profile.contact.email?<a class="button" href={`mailto:${profile.contact.email}`}>Start a conversation &#8599;</a>:<p class="contact-note">Public contact details are not currently listed.</p>}{profile.contact.linkedin&&<a href={profile.contact.linkedin}>LinkedIn</a>}{profile.contact.github&&<a href={profile.contact.github}>GitHub</a>}</div></section>
<script>
const explanations=['Web Application — Responsive interfaces make application workflows accessible to users.','APIs — Explicit request and response contracts connect interfaces with application capabilities.','Services — Focused business operations coordinate work and asynchronous processing.','Data — Application data is stored and retrieved through deliberate access boundaries.'];document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('.stage').forEach(button=>button.onclick=()=>{document.querySelectorAll('.stage').forEach(b=>b.setAttribute('aria-pressed','false'));button.setAttribute('aria-pressed','true');document.querySelector('#stage-description')!.textContent=explanations[Number(button.dataset.stage)];});const sample=document.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('#sample')!;const request=document.querySelector('#request')!;const response=document.querySelector('#response')!;const status=document.querySelector('#demo-status')!;const form=document.querySelector<HTMLFormElement>('#demo-form')!;const samples={valid:{title:'Synthetic task',quantity:2},invalid:{title:'',quantity:-1}};const selected=()=>samples[sample.value as keyof typeof samples];sample.onchange=()=>{request.textContent=JSON.stringify(selected(),null,2);response.textContent='No response yet.';status.textContent='Ready to validate a sample.';};form.onsubmit=e=>{e.preventDefault();const value=selected();const errors=[];if(!value.title.trim())errors.push('Title is required.');if(!Number.isInteger(value.quantity)||value.quantity<=0)errors.push('Quantity must be a positive integer.');response.textContent=JSON.stringify(errors.length?{status:400,errors}:{status:200,result:{...value,state:'accepted',synthetic:true}},null,2);status.textContent=errors.length?'Validation failed. Service was not invoked.':'Validation passed. Synthetic service response created.';};form.onreset=()=>{sample.value='valid';request.textContent=JSON.stringify(samples.valid,null,2);response.textContent='No response yet.';status.textContent='Ready to validate a sample.';};
</script></Layout>
